    "done_when": "Start from the qualifying weak-110 receipt driver at docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/repaired-remeasure-receipt/measure.py. A committed driver under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/certificate-ladder-500-1000-probe/ runs as ONE H200 job: RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch to betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, --mem=192G, --time=01:00:00, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv. That submission is a separate job on the H200 node, not a step of the fleet allocation the HOST line describes, and it is authorised; never srun or salloc. Submit for real and read squeue after a minute; only if it is still PENDING on a resource or configuration reason, resubmit to titan (--partition=titan --gres=gpu:1) and say so. Inside the job, the rows weak-rotation-reactor-static, moderate-rotation-conventional-static and strong-rotation-compact-static at requested cells -1000 and diverted-single-null at -500 run sequentially with clip_mode=exact passed explicitly, from the production seed, with the first-moment centroid row imposed, each row under its own bound of 12 minutes so one compile blow-up cannot consume the job, and each row receipt persisted as it lands. Each row records its realised cell count, compile seconds separately from solve seconds, the compiled program size where the driver can read it, peak host RSS, and either the section 3 clauses (max solved-minus-analytic over span against ten times 1.1e-4, axis error in pitches against 0.1, boundary level over span against 1e-3, compensating field amplitudes, terminal global and row residuals against 1e-12) or the exact failure: compile abort text, timeout at the bound, or a refusal before lowering. A row that solves gets a line-contour panel of solved over analytic on shared physical levels and the difference, both null sets, the wall, and residual and converged flag in the caption. The report /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-certificate-ladder-500-1000-probe.md tables each row as solved, compile-failed, timed-out or refused, with the figures above; the fragment docs/evidence/fragments/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/cco-certificate-ladder-500-1000-probe.html carries the table and any panels with project-absolute src. A failed row is a valid result and is reported as measured; no source under nova/ is edited. Keep scratch under the run directory, not /tmp, which is at 91 percent on the fleet node. Once the job is admitted, commit, write status waiting with the sacct probe as wait_probe and the job id in wait_condition, and end the turn; the recovery sweep resumes you when the job is terminal. This gate measures only this node; a failure outside its scope goes under follow_ons.",
